# Minimum allowed overall Rust coverage percentages.
# Update these only after an intentional, reviewed change lands and the new
# floor is accepted as the repository baseline — either a coverage improvement
# or a measurement-set change (e.g. relocating inline test modules into tests/
# directories, which cargo-llvm-cov excludes from the report by default, or
# excluding the untestable Tauri glue layer via COVERAGE_IGNORE_REGEX).
#
# Lowered from 96.62 → 96.55 with the G3 Google OAuth implementation
# (calendar/google.rs, calendar/google_token.rs, services/sync.rs), then to
# 96.42/94.44/93.19 when google.rs's inline test module moved to
# calendar/google/tests.rs to respect the 1000-line file cap (test code left
# the measured set; production coverage unchanged — same effect as the
# crud/schedule tests relocation).
# Remaining uncovered lines are all verified untestable:
#   - option_env!() Some branch (compile-time env vars; absent in test builds)
#   - OS-level failure paths: TcpListener::bind, set_nonblocking, accept errors,
#     stream read errors, URL parse of adversarial path
#   - oauth2 client-build error in parse_and_exchange (same creds used for
#     begin_auth and exchange; can't have one succeed while the other fails)
#   - write_all failure after successful open (requires disk full/readonly FS)
#   - unimplemented!() stubs in test-only mock structs (FailingSync in sync.rs)
#   - unreachable `other => panic!` arms in test match expressions
#
# Regions were temporarily lowered 94.44 → 94.35 while the sync-trace
# instrumentation (minute-grid + provider-precision merge investigation) sat
# in the tree; after stripping the trace hunks the floors were re-raised to
# the new actuals (lines 96.54, regions 94.47). One known permanently
# uncovered region remains from that unit: the unreachable duration_trunc
# error closure in slot_finder.rs (cannot fail with a 1-minute grid).
# Branches floor stays below actual (~94.3) on purpose — the overall-branch
# measurement flakes by ~1 branch in concurrent-test code.
#
# Lines lowered 96.54 → 96.44 by the migrations 001–008 squash: collapsing the
# eight pre-release migration modules into a single full-schema migration_001
# removed ~130 lines of fully-covered DDL from the measured set, mechanically
# lowering the overall average (the deleted lines were ~100% covered, pulling the
# mean up). Regions dropped the same way (94.47 → 94.30); branches (94.24) still
# clear their floor. migration_001 itself is 100% covered — no new uncovered code.

BASELINE_LINES_PCT=96.44
BASELINE_REGIONS_PCT=94.30
BASELINE_BRANCHES_PCT=93.19
